# Close Terminals & Free Ports (Strict)

Closing a terminal pane is **not** enough. Orphan Node/Vite processes often keep listening. Before every final reply, stop what you started **and** free the app ports.

## Ports (LevelUp)

| Service | Port |
|---------|------|
| API (`api/`) | **3000** |
| Web / Vite (`web/`) | **5173** |

Do **not** leave **3000** or **5173** occupied after your turn if you started anything that bound them.

## Prefer External Dev Servers

- The user runs long-lived `npm run dev` in an **external** terminal. Prefer that.
- Do **not** start persistent API/web servers in Cursor integrated terminals unless a short verification requires it.
- Prefer one-shot checks (`curl`, `npm run build`, `npx tsc`, tests) over keeping `dev` running.

## Required End-of-Turn Checklist

1. Stop every process/job **you** started this chat (dev, watch, background shells).
2. If you used or may have bound **3000** or **5173**, **force-free those ports** (see below) — even if you already closed the terminal window.
3. Confirm listeners are gone before the final message.
4. Never rely on the user to clean up.

## Force-Free Ports (Windows / PowerShell)

Run before ending the turn whenever 3000/5173 may be held by agent work:

```powershell
foreach ($port in 3000, 5173) {
  Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort $port -State Listen -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
    Select-Object -ExpandProperty OwningProcess -Unique |
    ForEach-Object { Stop-Process -Id $_ -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue }
}
```

Fallback if `Get-NetTCPConnection` is unavailable:

```powershell
netstat -ano | findstr ":3000 :5173"
# then: Stop-Process -Id <PID> -Force
```

Killing the terminal session PID alone is insufficient when children keep the port.

## Exceptions

- Leave a process running **only** if the user explicitly asks (e.g. "leave the server running").
- Do **not** kill listeners on 3000/5173 that the user already had running in an **external** terminal **unless** you (or an orphan from this chat) are what is holding the port, or the user asked you to free it.
- Postgres on **5432** (Docker) is out of scope — do not stop the DB container unless asked.
